Chapter: NormalizeEq

 Stage 3 of the proof system: a definitional-equality normalizer.
 Before the propositional-equality check runs, each side of a value
 `===` is reduced by delta (unfold a function call to its body) and
 iota (reduce a when-match whose scrutinee is a constructor). So
 `flip On` reduces to `Off` (delta flip, then iota the match), and
 `id-bit On` reduces to `On` (delta). Each claim then checks by Refl
 against the reduced normal form. The negative guard lives in
 codex/test/errors/normalize-false.

Section: Terms

  Bit =
   | On
   | Off

  flip : Bit -> Bit
  flip (b) = when b
   is On -> Off
   is Off -> On

  id-bit : Bit -> Bit
  id-bit (x) = x

  claim flip-on : flip On === Off
  proof flip-on = Refl
  qed

  claim flip-off : flip Off === On
  proof flip-off = Refl
  qed

  claim id-on : id-bit On === On
  proof id-on = Refl
  qed

  claim flip-twice : flip (flip On) === On
  proof flip-twice = Refl
  qed

Section: Main

  opening : [Console] Nothing
  opening = act
   print-line-uni "normalize-eq ok"
  end
